{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"RRQIy7gtLrg1"},"source":["# Python Programming for Data Science – Assignment 1\n","\n","**Name:** Denishay Mitchell Williams\n","\n","This workbook contains the completed solutions for Assignment 1. The code is kept clear and concise, with comments added only where they help explain the method."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"metadata":{"id":"6wBoXdKvLrg4","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1780553576143,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":707,"user":{"displayName":"Neuro Shay","userId":"14197004764472464475"}}},"outputs":[],"source":["## Let's import the libraries we are going to use later on\n","import numpy as np\n","import pandas as pd\n","\n","# Let's set the precision for NumPy and Pandas\n","np.set_printoptions(precision=3)\n","pd.options.display.float_format = '{:,.2f}'.format"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"Q32pCKq-Lrg4"},"source":["## Exercises on Data Structures"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"jG4V9SiFLrg5"},"source":["### 1. Compute statistics on a Python list\n","Given the following list\n","```\n","l = [12, 45, 12, 999, 10, 8, 76, 20, 10, 10, 7, 70, 17]\n","```\n","Compute the mean, the median and the standard deviation of the values in the list, using only built-in functionalities of python (no imported libraries, no NumPy or Pandas)"]},{"cell_type":"code","source":[],"metadata":{"id":"II_AwwDGMZs6","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1780553576153,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":1,"user":{"displayName":"Neuro Shay","userId":"14197004764472464475"}}},"execution_count":1,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":2,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"2isR_rNULrg5","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1780553576175,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":17,"user":{"displayName":"Neuro Shay","userId":"14197004764472464475"}},"outputId":"769ea175-1762-4af8-a39b-054927e52b65"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Mean: 99.6923076923077\n","Median: 12\n","Standard deviation: 260.6044407837537\n"]}],"source":["l = [12, 45, 12, 999, 10, 8, 76, 20, 10, 10, 7, 70, 17]\n","\n","# Mean\n","n = len(l)\n","mean = sum(l) / n\n","\n","# Median\n","sorted_l = sorted(l)\n","\n","if n % 2 == 1:\n","    median = sorted_l[n // 2]\n","else:\n","    median = (sorted_l[n // 2 - 1] + sorted_l[n // 2]) / 2\n","\n","# Population standard deviation\n","std_dev = (sum((x - mean) ** 2 for x in l) / n) ** 0.5\n","\n","print(\"Mean:\", mean)\n","print(\"Median:\", median)\n","print(\"Standard deviation:\", std_dev)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"t0__QJCaLrg5"},"source":["### 2A. Create a dictionary from a list of tuples (records)\n","\n","Given the following list of tuples, each one holding a record\n","```\n","records = [\n","    ('author', 'title', 'publication_year', 'page_count'),\n","    ('J. R. R. Tolkien', 'The Fellowship of the Ring', 1954, 398),\n","    ('J. K. Rowling', 'Harry Potter and the Philosopher\\'s stone', 1996, 223),\n","    ('Evelyn Waugh', 'Brideshead Revisited', 1945, 402),\n","    ('Philip K. Dick', 'Ubik', 1969, 202),\n","    ('Thomas Pynchon', \"Gravity's Rainbow\", 1973, 760),\n","    ('Stephen King', 'The Stand', 1978, 829)\n","]\n","```\n","Convert them into a list of dictionaries, using the first tuple as keys for all the dictionaries and all the other tuples as values, one per dictionary.\n","Expected result:\n","\n","```\n","books = [{'author': 'J. R. R. Tolkien',\n","  'title': 'The Fellowship of the Ring',\n","  'publication_year': 1954,\n","  'page_count': 398},\n"," {'author': 'J. K. Rowling',\n","  'title': \"Harry Potter and the Philosopher's stone\",\n","  'publication_year': 1996,\n","  'page_count': 223},\n"," {'author': 'Evelyn Waugh',\n","  'title': 'Brideshead Revisited',\n","  'publication_year': 1945,\n","  'page_count': 402},\n"," {'author': 'Philip K. Dick',\n","  'title': 'Ubik',\n","  'publication_year': 1969,\n","  'page_count': 202},\n"," {'author': 'Thomas Pynchon',\n","  'title': \"Gravity's Rainbow\",\n","  'publication_year': 1973,\n","  'page_count': 760},\n"," {'author': 'Stephen King',\n","  'title': 'The Stand',\n","  'publication_year': 1978,\n","  'page_count': 829}]\n","```"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":3,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"DMenjUdKLrg5","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1780553576200,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":11,"user":{"displayName":"Neuro Shay","userId":"14197004764472464475"}},"outputId":"b89c3c5b-d703-4138-d599-6d56aac6dc75"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":["[{'author': 'J. R. R. Tolkien',\n","  'title': 'The Fellowship of the Ring',\n","  'publication_year': 1954,\n","  'page_count': 398},\n"," {'author': 'J. K. Rowling',\n","  'title': \"Harry Potter and the Philosopher's stone\",\n","  'publication_year': 1996,\n","  'page_count': 223},\n"," {'author': 'Evelyn Waugh',\n","  'title': 'Brideshead Revisited',\n","  'publication_year': 1945,\n","  'page_count': 402},\n"," {'author': 'Philip K. Dick',\n","  'title': 'Ubik',\n","  'publication_year': 1969,\n","  'page_count': 202},\n"," {'author': 'Thomas Pynchon',\n","  'title': \"Gravity's Rainbow\",\n","  'publication_year': 1973,\n","  'page_count': 760},\n"," {'author': 'Stephen King',\n","  'title': 'The Stand',\n","  'publication_year': 1978,\n","  'page_count': 829}]"]},"metadata":{},"execution_count":3}],"source":["records = [\n","    ('author', 'title', 'publication_year', 'page_count'),\n","    ('J. R. R. Tolkien', 'The Fellowship of the Ring', 1954, 398),\n","    ('J. K. Rowling', 'Harry Potter and the Philosopher\\'s stone', 1996, 223),\n","    ('Evelyn Waugh', 'Brideshead Revisited', 1945, 402),\n","    ('Philip K. Dick', 'Ubik', 1969, 202),\n","    ('Thomas Pynchon', \"Gravity's Rainbow\", 1973, 760),\n","    ('Stephen King', 'The Stand', 1978, 829)\n","]\n","\n","# The first tuple contains the dictionary keys.\n","keys = records[0]\n","\n","# Each remaining tuple is converted into one dictionary.\n","books = [dict(zip(keys, record)) for record in records[1:]]\n","\n","books"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"dTKi0TXSLrg6"},"source":["### 2B. Dictionary manipulation\n","Write a function that takes the dictionary like `books` and return the author whose book has the highest page count.\n","\n","Apply the function to `books` to verify that it works correctly"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":4,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":36},"id":"j37Z7UNFLrg6","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1780553576230,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":20,"user":{"displayName":"Neuro Shay","userId":"14197004764472464475"}},"outputId":"8d4dd64c-0999-4a94-84da-da5d7807338f"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":["'Stephen King'"],"application/vnd.google.colaboratory.intrinsic+json":{"type":"string"}},"metadata":{},"execution_count":4}],"source":["def author_highest_page_count(books):\n","    \"\"\"Return the author whose book has the highest page count.\"\"\"\n","    highest_book = books[0]\n","\n","    for book in books:\n","        if book['page_count'] > highest_book['page_count']:\n","            highest_book = book\n","\n","    return highest_book['author']\n","\n","author_highest_page_count(books)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"563w_DyiLrg6"},"source":["## Exercises on Numpy"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"W88ueJhbLrg6"},"source":["For these exercises we will work on the IRIS dataset, a very popular multivariate dataset for data anaylisis, first introduced by Ronald Fisher in 1936.\n","\n","See more about the IRIS dataset heare: https://archive.ics.uci.edu/ml/datasets/Iris\n","\n","The data source is the file `iris.data` retrieved from the Web. It contains the data for this example in comma separated values (CSV) format. The number of columns is 5 and the number of rows is 150. The data set is composed of 50 samples from each of three species of Iris Flower: Iris Setosa, Iris Virginica and Iris Versicolor. Four features were measured from each sample: the length and the width of the sepals and petals, in centimetres. Based on the combination of these four features, Fisher developed a linear discriminant model to distinguish the species one from each other.\n","\n","The variables are:\n","\n","    sepal_length: Sepal length, in centimeters.\n","    sepal_width: Sepal width, in centimeters.\n","    petal_length: Petal length, in centimeters.\n","    petal_width: Petal width, in centimeters.\n","\n","The three categories of Irises are: 'Iris Setosa', 'Iris Versicolor', and 'Iris Virginica'.\n","\n","Let's first import the `iris` dataset as a 1-dimensional array of tuples."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":5,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"fZUz_W0NLrg6","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1780553577173,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":943,"user":{"displayName":"Neuro Shay","userId":"14197004764472464475"}},"outputId":"8491e45b-3a1e-46d6-8ab3-b016621d6e41"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":["array([(5.1, 3.5, 1.4, 0.2, 'Iris-setosa'),\n","       (4.9, 3. , 1.4, 0.2, 'Iris-setosa'),\n","       (4.7, 3.2, 1.3, 0.2, 'Iris-setosa'),\n","       (4.6, 3.1, 1.5, 0.2, 'Iris-setosa'),\n","       (5. , 3.6, 1.4, 0.2, 'Iris-setosa'),\n","       (5.4, 3.9, 1.7, 0.4, 'Iris-setosa'),\n","       (4.6, 3.4, 1.4, 0.3, 'Iris-setosa'),\n","       (5. , 3.4, 1.5, 0.2, 'Iris-setosa'),\n","       (4.4, 2.9, 1.4, 0.2, 'Iris-setosa'),\n","       (4.9, 3.1, 1.5, 0.1, 'Iris-setosa'),\n","       (5.4, 3.7, 1.5, 0.2, 'Iris-setosa'),\n","       (4.8, 3.4, 1.6, 0.2, 'Iris-setosa'),\n","       (4.8, 3. , 1.4, 0.1, 'Iris-setosa'),\n","       (4.3, 3. , 1.1, 0.1, 'Iris-setosa'),\n","       (5.8, 4. , 1.2, 0.2, 'Iris-setosa'),\n","       (5.7, 4.4, 1.5, 0.4, 'Iris-setosa'),\n","       (5.4, 3.9, 1.3, 0.4, 'Iris-setosa'),\n","       (5.1, 3.5, 